          explanation: 'Example: You have $10,000 in stock (cost basis $2,000). If you sell and donate cash, you pay $1,904 in capital gains tax and donate $8,096. If you donate the stock directly, the charity gets $10,000 and you avoid the $1,904 tax. Same generosity, but $1,904 more for the charity (or less out of your pocket).'
