        {myth:'Smart investors can time the market',truth:'A Nobel Prize-winning study found market timing explained only 2% of portfolio returns, while asset allocation explained 94%.',explanation:'Even professionals can\'t consistently time the market, 92% of active fund managers underperform their benchmark over 15 years. Staying invested in the right mix beats jumping in and out.'},
        {myth:'I won\'t panic, I\'m rational about money',truth:'Neuroimaging shows financial losses activate the same brain regions as physical pain (the amygdala), an involuntary response, not a choice.',explanation:'Without predetermined systems (an Investment Policy Statement, automation, or an advisor), virtually everyone panics eventually. Rules built in advance protect you from your own wiring.'},
        {myth:'Checking my portfolio frequently helps me stay informed',truth:'Frequent portfolio checking increases trading activity and reduces returns, daily checkers earn 2-3% less than quarterly checkers.',explanation:'Each check triggers an emotional evaluation that can lead to action, and most actions reduce returns. Less monitoring is genuinely more profitable.'}
