      { takeaway: 'The behavior gap costs 3-4% per year', detail: 'DALBAR shows the average investor earns 7.13% while the S&P 500 returns 10.65%. Over 30 years on $100K, this gap costs $1.3M. The gap comes from panic selling, performance chasing, and overtrading, not from bad investment selection.' },
      { takeaway: 'Systems beat willpower every time', detail: 'Write an Investment Policy Statement, automate contributions and rebalancing, and reduce portfolio check frequency. Written pre-commitments increase follow-through by 40%. The best investors remove themselves from as many decisions as possible.' },
      { takeaway: 'Behavioral coaching is the most valuable advisor service', detail: 'Vanguard values behavioral coaching at 1.5%/year, more than tax optimization, rebalancing, and all other services combined. An advisor who prevents one panic sell per decade pays for themselves many times over.' }
