        { term: 'Direct Indexing', definition: 'Owning individual stocks that compose an index (instead of an index fund) to enable stock-level tax-loss harvesting and ESG customization. Technology has reduced the cost from $1M+ minimums to $100K-$500K.', example: 'A direct indexing account holds 500 individual stocks replicating the S&P 500. When 50 stocks have losses while the index is up, all 50 losses are harvested, generating 2-3x more tax savings than holding a single S&P 500 ETF.' },
        { term: 'Tokenization', definition: 'Converting ownership of an asset (real estate, art, private equity) into digital tokens on a blockchain. Enables fractional ownership, 24/7 trading, and reduced transaction costs.', example: 'A $10M commercial building is tokenized into 100,000 tokens at $100 each. An investor can buy 10 tokens ($1,000) to own 0.01% of the building, receiving proportional rental income and appreciation, previously impossible without $500K+ minimums.' }
