      ['Should I use a robo-advisor or human advisor?','Both. Use a robo-advisor for core portfolio management (daily rebalancing, TLH, allocation) at 0.25%. Use a fee-only human advisor for complex needs (estate planning, tax strategy, behavioral coaching, life transitions) at a flat fee. 60% of robo-advisor users already supplement with human advice. The hybrid model provides the best of both at reasonable cost.'],
      ['Is automated tax-loss harvesting worth it?','Absolutely. Wealthfront reports 1.5-2.0% annual benefit. On a $500K portfolio, that\'s $7,500-$10,000/year in tax savings, versus the $1,250 robo-advisor fee. TLH alone generates a 6-8x return on the management fee. No human advisor can scan every position daily and execute swaps instantly.'],
      ['What is the risk of blockchain-based investments?','Significant risks remain: regulatory uncertainty (SEC vs. crypto industry), security vulnerabilities (exchange hacks), project failures (95%+ of crypto projects fail), and fraud (FTX, Terra/Luna). Tokenized real-world assets (real estate, bonds) offer more promise than speculative cryptocurrencies, but the regulatory framework is still developing. Limit blockchain exposure to 1-5% of portfolio and stick to regulated platforms.'],
      ['Will AI replace financial advisors?','AI will replace the analytical tasks advisors perform (portfolio optimization, tax planning, scenario analysis) but not the human elements (behavioral coaching, emotional support during market panics, complex family dynamics, life transition guidance). The best advisors will use AI to enhance their capabilities, spending less time on spreadsheets and more time on client relationships.']
