      'Robo-advisor + direct indexing for daily management, fee-only planner for human advice, thoughtful emerging tech adoption, scoring 9/9. Total cost: ~$5,000-$6,500/year with $10K-$14K in TLH benefits. This is the optimal wealth management stack for the technology era.',
      'Technology has democratized wealth management: professional-grade portfolio management at 0.25%, daily tax-loss harvesting that adds 1.5-2.0%, direct indexing previously reserved for ultra-wealthy, and AI planning that analyzes thousands of variables instantly. But technology is a tool, not a replacement for human judgment. The optimal stack combines algorithmic efficiency (robo-advisors, TLH, AI) with human wisdom (fee-only planners, behavioral coaching), delivering better outcomes at lower cost than either approach alone.'
